PHASE 5 — SUGAR CALCULATION ENGINE

Objective

Implement reliable sugar intake analysis using existing verified nutrient data.

5.1 Nutrient Separation

Maintain separate calculations for:

- Total Sugars.
- Added Sugars.

Do not infer Added Sugars from Total Sugars.

Do not infer Total Sugars from Carbohydrates.

5.2 Required Outputs

Where supported:

- Total Sugar per food.
- Total Sugar per meal.
- Total Sugar per day.
- Added Sugar per food.
- Added Sugar per meal.
- Added Sugar per day.
- Naturally occurring sugar, only when it can be accurately determined.
- Percentage of energy from Added Sugars.
- Reference comparison.
- Data completeness.
- Warnings.

5.3 Missing Added Sugar Data

When Added Sugar data are unavailable:

- Total Sugar calculation may still be available.
- Added Sugar calculation must be marked unavailable or incomplete.
- Never assume Added Sugar = 0.
- Never infer Added Sugar based solely on food category.
- Never infer Added Sugar from Total Sugar.
- Do not automatically classify every sugar in a food as Added Sugar.

For recipes, Added Sugar may only be calculated when the ingredients and their Added Sugar values are sufficiently documented.

5.4 Energy Calculations

Use the existing energy calculation infrastructure where possible.

If calculating percentage energy:

- Use 4 kcal per gram of sugar, where applicable.
- Validate total energy.
- Use the correct denominator.
- Handle zero energy safely.
- Document the calculation.
- Do not calculate percentages from incomplete or invalid data without clearly indicating the limitation.

